===Etymology===
1)Schröer suggests a combination of {{etyl|he|en}} [[מֵפִיץ]] ''mêp̄îṣ'' ("destroyer") and [[ט֫פֶל]] ''tōp̄el'' ("liar") from [[ט֫פֶל שֶׁ֫קֶר]] ''tōp̄el šeqer'' ("falsehood plasterer"), see [[שֶׁקֶר]]; compare Job xiii:4).<ref name="Englische Studien">[Eugen Kölbing].</ref>

2)[[מֵפִיץ]] ''mêp̄îṣ'' (''to bring down''),+ [[תופת]] (''Topheth'') ,+  heles (''Ancient Greece").  מפיץ שיטנת יוון הקדומה meaning to spread Ancient Greece topheth*(flame).
*Topheth see - 2 Kings,chapter 23/10

